{"title":"2006 SMT/Team Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da00c18a76c1e423657fa98f5b4cef6295b164b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis. Cone <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is formed when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is rotated about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis, and cone <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is formed when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is rotated about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis. If the volume of cone <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> minus the volume fo cone <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/67390af1664de6706fa16389048486f661be0d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />, find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a given sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d1518935adf51307feaca20a89ba97ceb7ecad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{S_1, S_2, \\cdots S_k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />, for terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b21b36bfc3bad4b81f5aed2c6f5613bc98403ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858fa46fef823346d39f159602ad9517dfa74461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n=\\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}i\\cdot S_{n-i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"126\" height=\"50\" />. For example, if the first two elements are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, the third entry would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/512973521b51f5891f16520741a4516df9046afe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot3+2\\cdot2=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />, and the fourth would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/05752d81b79244a560078286427185a8e8911fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot7+2\\cdot3+3\\cdot2=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"14\" />, and so on. Given that a sequence of integers having this form starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732bbea24ba23515adc430dca825bc7a77a0ec0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\text{th}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> element is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782dd7447f84ce6adcf7945b86038e379c618f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, what is the second element?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangle has altitudes of lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the maximum length of the third altitude?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189e3ce6d1b3191e48b16849e0a5dcb1494f7d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/9176f74a1c881cea97c7d8bf2a0ae691bed66baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. The expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff50a30b60b657c1064cd8cfc8ec5f57b2f89eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^6+y^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> can be written as a polynomial in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. What is this polynomial?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There exist two positive numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6fd853d243ae59978f26586200d07d86b7049a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\arccos(\\tan(\\arcsin(x))))=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />. Find the product of the two possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d4bfb507567a9edd358ffe948012eecb2e98c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16^n+4^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> is equivalent to the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8b8388b2d56eed7462c910f8d609623978781a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^{p(n)}-1)/(2^{q(n)}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/02236d6b258335c6c5a4da933d9597081c28d7ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> are functions and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d852a2d05b317248c6aeac251083aec6d56cff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p(n)}{q(n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"36\" height=\"43\" /> is constant. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793072c443944c34d7c7aaaf75be2845160cb2d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(2006)-q(2006)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tuples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/79248a54925980615cae92d606b15170ec722f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=3000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a0dc1d53202f0003849a81d76e5555b1ee251a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />. If one of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tuples is chosen at random, what's the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86ea9490aef21beb354a6852aa52d9f40cf29503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Evaluate: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/b/9bb178091fa52752256048080070352cf7c0f320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=n^2}^{(n+1)^2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"110\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. The medians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a5dab0650ea78f80ca12d62afe83905de42ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MC}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/50101837fd77dcec7cef9fba6c282772c4d29d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{NB}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> intersect at a right angle. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c3af7e805c765814514d530d617a3787d7684b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{AB}{BC}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"65\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> odd positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f300d1b990fade638d08a9630914d1775192d856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n^3+m}{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"59\" height=\"40\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be705e2717b971aa9bfa318432928a7d5f8b7892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=c_{2006}x^{2006}+c_{2005}x^{2005}+\\cdots+c_1x+c_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"358\" height=\"19\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a6caee096f94ac38ffd5d5115854e5d638755f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\cdots, r_{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"11\" />. The coefficients satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16caf8ad4f02bf51e51dadfa0ee0bf54aa9238c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2i\\frac{c_i}{c_{2006}-i}=2j\\frac{c_j}{c_{2006}-j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"193\" height=\"36\" /> for all pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb4e0a5d7ff5b6f537df2afb0ca4382ad1cf311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le i, j\\le2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74cfdf4225018f4cf09dc3323b511321493bffa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i\\not=j, i=1, j=1}^{2006}\\frac{r_i}{r_j}=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"136\" height=\"53\" />, determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/2219b42eeeb6394fbaa4cd0d7a32f93c37c225f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{2006}r_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"42\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>(Note: The original problem asked for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b88dfc707d3a77795396f433c3269acd42a62c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{2006}(r_1+r_2+\\cdots+r_{2006})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"193\" height=\"50\" />, but the official solution makes it clear that the actual desired sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/2219b42eeeb6394fbaa4cd0d7a32f93c37c225f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{2006}r_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"42\" height=\"50\" />.)</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the total number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />-tuples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6deb18caa3fc9bf406dfaaca2ea74b2f233a2c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n_1, n_2, \\cdots, n_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/257d6f79782b9ed19eef03fdef75f08203540a17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{i+1}\\ge n_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> regular polygons with numbers of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7889ea4498c373cc43edc1a2124042b31b00f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1, n_2, \\cdots n_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> respectively will fit into a tesselation at a point. That is, the sum of one interior angle from each of the polygons is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9506d61661a7d046ee93b381ddb704684ffd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^\\circ$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A ray is drawn from the origin tangent to the graph of the upper part of the hyperbola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471d5ae6fd2e0dd69c300c92f11c97b772b147ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2=x^2-x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> in the first quadrant. This ray makes an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a3b34841a0696e4e3afc4fda90bda98eead51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43de2f70dc75a938eeab6ea251741a53d1d410fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2006}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd99228146175c61e5cca6be965d17c918d45cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> denote the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b6349f396b5c821b823382c3f09a70d4800eee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\text{th}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> composite integer so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/52755ed899752a4f278f6ca7e915a82822ebec73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{c_i\\}=4, 6, 8, 9\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. Compute \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c5168f668672efe73a13967634642227f8b1b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{i=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{c_i^2}{c_i^2-1}\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>(Hint: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/9175e1ecc553e8425decfb3b3d5b87217b12b561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n^2}=\\frac{\\pi^2}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"96\" height=\"48\" />)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>(Note: The original hint stated that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb0cb79e24542829b697a26a4b0c8f74391efbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{n^2}=\\frac{\\pi^2}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"96\" height=\"48\" />.)</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stanford_Mathematics_Tournament\" title=\"Stanford Mathematics Tournament\">Stanford Mathematics Tournament</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stanford_Mathematics_Tournament_Problems\" title=\"Stanford Mathematics Tournament Problems\">SMT Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT\" title=\"2006 SMT\">2006 SMT</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Team\" title=\"2006 SMT/Team\">2006 SMT/Team</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018052743\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 542/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17197/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11176:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018052743 and revision id 47185. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}